  // top. The water runs off the pillar's top as a thin flowing skirt, drops down all four sides as
  // falling columns and spreads out where it lands. Verified by the first shot after the pour:
  // the pillar wears a light-blue cap and blue falling faces. Poured shallow water is faint from
  // steep angles (little thickness to absorb over), so the skirt shots are low and close.
  // still_pond is the control: it is taken BEFORE any edit, at ponds.json's lake_across pose, and
  // must match a pre-SH-14 run, since still water bakes flow code 0.
